.TH PHP-SERVER 1 "November 2026" "php-rust" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
php-server \- standalone PHP web server (php \-S work-alike)
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B php-server
.RI [ options ]
.RI [ ROUTER.php ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B php-server
is the web SAPI of the php-rust project: a standalone HTTP server that
serves a document root and executes PHP requests through the phpr
engine. It speaks plain HTTP \(em it is
.B not
a FastCGI backend and does not implement the FPM protocol, so it
cannot replace php*-fpm behind nginx/Apache
.BR fastcgi_pass .
Front it with any reverse proxy over HTTP instead.
.PP
Two modes are selected at startup:
.TP
.B cli-server (default)
Byte-faithful work-alike of the reference
.BR "php \-S" :
one thread, sequential request handling, honours a
.I ROUTER.php
router script.
.TP
.B \-\-axum
Axum front end with a pool of N OS worker threads sharing one FIFO
queue; each request runs on a fresh VM (no state leaks between
requests). Note: a router script is
.B not
honoured in this mode; single-process SIGTERM/SIGINT drains cleanly.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI \-\-host " HOST"
Listen address (default: 127.0.0.1).
.TP
.BI \-\-port " PORT"
Listen port (default: 8080).
.TP
.BI \-\-docroot " DIR" | " \-t DIR"
Document root; resolved to its canonical path and made the process
working directory (default: current directory).
.TP
.BI \-\-workers " N"
Worker count in \-\-axum mode; 0 means one worker per CPU (ignored by
the cli-server mode).
.TP
.B \-\-tier0
Axum-only diagnostic baseline: static 200 response, no pool, no VM.
.TP
.B \-\-help
Usage summary.
.SH SYSTEMD
On Debian the
.B phpr\-server.service
unit runs this program in \-\-axum mode as the
.B www\-data
user, with settings taken from
.IR /etc/default/phpr\-server
(PHPR_HOST, PHPR_PORT, PHPR_DOCROOT, PHPR_WORKERS). Enabled by default
\(em see
.BR systemctl (1).
.SH SEE ALSO
The CLI interpreter:
.BR phpr (1).
.SH AUTHOR
php-rust by Francesco Tinti. This manual page was written for the
Debian project.
